# Concept guest voice

Guest-visible copy in `src/concepts/` must speak as the business.

Do **not** put studio, research, or website-meta narration in headings, body, notices, captions, alts, aria-labels, or footers. Examples of banned voice:

- "this concept / prototype / screen demonstrates"
- "illustrative flavour / queue / structure / sample"
- "generated illustration — not a photograph"
- "from their public website" / research-file framing
- "Mourne Made" or "independent concept by…" outside the shell banner
- Design-evaluation or elevation-method language
- Research audit chrome mistaken for transparency: `· read 6 August 2026`,
  `shown as "10 months ago"`, `their words, not ours`, `freshest source`,
  `mid-point of the late-1960s BBC archive date`, `where it is verified from`,
  or dual-name findings phrased as research ("X on Facebook and Y on Main
  Street are the same shop")

Attribution on the guest layer stays light and useful — who spoke, and a
reasonable month/year or era (`Google review · October 2025`, `BBC · late
1960s`). Full read dates, elisions, and verification notes belong in
`research/`, code comments, and case-study Sources & limits.

Honesty belongs only in:

- `ConceptLayout` banner / `bannerNote`
- `research/`
- code comments
- transformation case-study Sources & limits

See also the three-layer honesty split in `docs/the-elevation-method.md`.

After editing concept copy, run `pnpm test:guest-voice` (also part of `pnpm build`).
